      "message": "It should be 8 not 9. I corrected the other comment but not this one. Will correct this one in the next patch set.\n\nThe reason it is 8 is because the expression is \"avg(hpcs.compute.cpu{id\u003d5}, 60) \u003e 3 times 3\". The alarm doesn\u0027t change to alarm until there have 2 * the number of periods where there are no metrics in any of the periods under evaluation. This works out to Periods * 3 - 1.\n\nThe API doc says:\n\nUNDETERMINED - No metrics for at least one of the subexpressions has been received in (period + 2) times periods (see below for definition of period and periods\n\nHowever this is incorrect. I\u0027ll have to update it.",
